S1v52pA4A8QAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==' /%3e%3c/svg%3e\" width=\"2202\" alt=\"Fourth\" data-srcset=\"/assets/static/four-john.82a2fbd.0cec6197a5b0b44122006cb0ddd0d5b0.png 480w, /assets/static/four-john.cbab2cf.0cec6197a5b0b44122006cb0ddd0d5b0.png 1024w, /assets/static/four-john.b344136.0cec6197a5b0b44122006cb0ddd0d5b0.png 2202w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 2202px) 100vw, 2202px\" data-src=\"/assets/static/four-john.b344136.0cec6197a5b0b44122006cb0ddd0d5b0.png\"><noscript><img class=\"g-image g-image--lazy g-image--loaded\" src=\"/assets/static/four-john.b344136.0cec6197a5b0b44122006cb0ddd0d5b0.png\" width=\"2202\" alt=\"Fourth\"></noscript></p>\n<p>After you set all settings for bucket, you have to make your bucket accessible. Go to <code class=\"language-text\">Your Bucket</code>-><code class=\"language-text\">Permissions</code>-><code class=\"language-text\">Bucket Policy</code> then paste it.</p>\n<pre class=\"language-json\"><code class=\"language-json\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token property\">\"Version\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"2012-10-17\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n    <span class=\"token property\">\"Statement\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"token property\">\"Sid\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"Allow Public Access to All Objects\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"token property\">\"Effect\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"Allow\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"token property\">\"Principal\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"*\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"token property\">\"Action\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"s3:GetObject\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n            <span class=\"token property\">\"Resource\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"arn:aws:s3::::john-wick/*\"</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>This will make your bucket accessible. <code class=\"language-text\">john-wick</code> is my bucket's name, so if you did it with another name you have to set it with that special name.</p>\n<h2 id=\"pushing-to-amazon-s3\"><a href=\"#pushing-to-amazon-s3\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"icon icon-link\"></span></a>Pushing to Amazon S3</h2>\n<p>In your <code class=\"language-text\">ReactJS</code> application, add </p>\n<pre class=\"language-json\"><code class=\"language-json\"><span class=\"token property\">\"deploy\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"aws s3 sync build/ s3://john-wick --acl public-read\"</span></code></pre>\n<p>into your <code class=\"language-text\">package.json</code>, this will send our <code class=\"language-text\">build/</code> directory into our <code class=\"language-text\">s3://john-wick</code> bucket.</p>\n<p>Before deploying, let's take our project's build with <code class=\"language-text\">npm run build</code></p>\n<p>After getting successfully build run <code class=\"language-text\">npm run deploy</code>.</p>\n<p>Our <code class=\"language-text\">build</code> directory is in our bucket, take a look at to the bucket. You will see like a page like below.</p>\n<p><img class=\"g-image g-image--lazy g-image--loading\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3csvg fill='none' viewBox='0 0 2560 1200' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink'%3e%3cdefs%3e%3cfilter id='__svg-blur-8740a737f